/**
@page api_specialized Specialized Modules
@brief Polling, loss networks, LQNs, non-product-form networks

These modules provide domain-specific functionality for specialized queueing applications.

@section spec_polling Polling Systems (matlab/src/api/polling/)

The polling module implements algorithms for polling systems with various
polling strategies (gated, exhaustive, k-limited).

@subsection spec_polling_functions Key Functions

- @ref polling_qsys_1limited.m "polling_qsys_1limited" - W=polling_qsys_1limited(arvMAPs,svcMAPs,switchMAPs)

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  polling_qsys_1limited(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> W=polling_qsys_1limited(arvMAPs,svcMAPs,switchMAPs)

- @ref polling_qsys_exhaustive.m "polling_qsys_exhaustive" - W=polling_qsys_exhaustive(arvMAPs,svcMAPs,switchMAPs)

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  polling_qsys_exhaustive(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> W=polling_qsys_exhaustive(arvMAPs,svcMAPs,switchMAPs)

- @ref polling_qsys_gated.m "polling_qsys_gated" - W=polling_qsys_gated(arvMAPs,svcMAPs,switchMAPs)

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  polling_qsys_gated(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> W=polling_qsys_gated(arvMAPs,svcMAPs,switchMAPs)


@section spec_npfqn Non-Product-Form Networks (matlab/src/api/npfqn/)

The npfqn module provides approximation methods for non-product-form queueing
networks that do not satisfy BCMP conditions.

@subsection spec_npfqn_functions Key Functions

- @ref npfqn_nonexp_approx.m "npfqn_nonexp_approx" - handler for non-exponential service and arrival processes

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [ST, gamma, nservers, rho, scva, scvs, eta] = npfqn_nonexp_approx(method, sn, ST, V, SCV, T, U, gamma, nservers)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>method</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>sn</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ST</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>V</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>SCV</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>T</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>U</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>gamma</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>nservers</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>ST</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>gamma</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>nservers</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rho</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>scva</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>scvs</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>eta</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> handler for non-exponential service and arrival processes

- @ref npfqn_traffic_merge_cs.m "npfqn_traffic_merge_cs" - Given a cell array of n MMAPs with arrivals of R classes, produces a new

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  npfqn_traffic_merge_cs(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Given a cell array of n MMAPs with arrivals of R classes, produces a new

- @ref npfqn_traffic_merge.m "npfqn_traffic_merge" - Given a cell array of n MMAPs with arrivals of R classes, produces a new

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  npfqn_traffic_merge(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Given a cell array of n MMAPs with arrivals of R classes, produces a new

- @ref npfqn_traffic_split_cs.m "npfqn_traffic_split_cs" - Given a MMAP, produces a new array after split and class switching

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  npfqn_traffic_split_cs(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Given a MMAP, produces a new array after split and class switching


@section spec_lossn Loss Networks (matlab/src/api/lossn/)

The lossn module implements algorithms for loss networks where arrivals can
be blocked when resources are unavailable.

@subsection spec_lossn_functions Key Functions

- @ref lossn_erlangfp.m "lossn_erlangfp" - Erlang fixed point approximation for loss networks

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [QLen, Loss, E, niter] = lossn_erlangfp(nu, A, C)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>nu</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>A</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  <tr><td>C</td><td>Parameter description</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>QLen</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Loss</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>E</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  <tr><td>niter</td><td>Return value</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Description:</b> Erlang fixed point approximation for loss networks


@section spec_lsn Layered Stochastic Networks (matlab/src/api/lsn/)

The lsn module provides algorithms for layered stochastic networks and
layered queueing networks (LQNs).

@subsection spec_lsn_functions Key Functions

- @ref lsn_max_multiplicity.m "lsn_max_multiplicity" - Computes the maximum multiplicity of nodes in a Layered Software Network

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  lsn_max_multiplicity(...)
  @endcode

  <b>Description:</b> Computes the maximum multiplicity of nodes in a Layered Software Network


@section spec_rl Reinforcement Learning (matlab/src/api/rl/)

The rl module provides reinforcement learning utilities for queueing control
and optimization problems.

